    {
      "id": "9c0d1f5a-5155-4603-a4f1-1f2e880b4bd1",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2864,
        1392
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 644,
        "height": 824,
        "content": "## Sort website contacts into role vs personal emails - with an audit log and monthly stale-domain retry\n\n**Who's it for:** anyone building a cold-outreach or lead-gen list who needs verified contact info without buying a data subscription, wants a real audit trail of every batch, and doesn't want \"no contact published\" to be a permanent dead end.\n\n**What it does:** reads company domains from a Google Sheet, runs the Apify Verified Website Contact Finder actor, then routes every result by quality: role addresses go straight to outreach, personal addresses are flagged for manual GDPR review, sites that publish nothing are marked, and unreachable sites retry next run. Every batch also gets summarized and logged as one audit row in a separate run_log tab - counts of each outcome, timestamped. A second, independent monthly schedule re-checks any domain still marked \"no contact published\" after 60 days and requeues it, since companies do eventually add a contact page - so this stops being a one-shot lookup and becomes something you can leave running for months.\n\n**Requirements:** an Apify account (pay-per-result, no subscription - the free account includes $5/month of platform credit to start) and a Google account for Sheets access. Uses the community node @apify/n8n-nodes-apify - install it from the nodes panel (search \"Apify\") first. Verified and Cloud-installable, works self-hosted too.\n\n**How to set up:** make a copy of the linked sheet (it already has the domain_contacts and run_log tabs), swap in your own domains, connect your Apify and Google Sheets credentials, replace the sheet reference in every node with your copy's ID, and activate the monthly schedule trigger if you want the stale-retry maintenance loop running unattended.\n\n**How to customize:** adjust the switch node's branch conditions, change the 60-day staleness window on the maintenance flow, or add more output columns to match your CRM's schema."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "0b74e2cf-f7e1-49d2-bf19-e87374ccb72f",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -928,
        1296
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 548,
        "height": 176,
        "content": "**Why 4 branches, not 1 list**\nA plain scraper returns one flat array of emails. This actor returns which are role vs personal, and whether a domain was unreachable vs genuinely empty — so this workflow can route each outcome differently instead of you sorting a spreadsheet by hand."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "009bd5d1-52ae-4642-8a28-91994cb22ff6",
      "name": "Prerequisites",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2816,
        2336
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 540,
        "height": 464,
        "content": "## What you'll need\n- A free Apify account (console.apify.com) - the actor itself is pay-per-result, no subscription, and the free account gives you $5/month of platform credit to start\n- A Google account you're happy connecting via OAuth for Sheets access\n- 5 minutes: this workflow has no manual coding, only credential setup and one copy-paste of a sheet ID\n\n**Two triggers, both need wiring:** the manual/schedule trigger at the top runs the everyday enrichment pass. The separate 'Monthly stale-recheck schedule' trigger lower down runs the maintenance loop - activate the workflow (not just test it) if you want that one to actually fire on its own each month.\n\n**New to n8n?** Every node below has a note explaining what it does and why it's shaped this way - click any node once to read its note in the right-hand panel."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d3f69268-52ba-4c6b-ac0b-55e91c1c3070",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2128,
        2144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 656,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "**Two systems, not one**\n\nThe top flow is the everyday enrichment pass. This bottom flow is independent maintenance: once a month it looks for domains marked \"no contact published\" more than 60 days ago and gives them another chance, since a company's contact page can appear well after the first check. Combined with the run_log audit trail above, this turns a one-shot lookup into something you could actually leave running unattended for months."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
